Spoilers...

Once you have the bell from your quest, why not cursing it and summoning lots
of undeads?
I tried it with a priest wielding a +5 vorpal: I boosted my hp up to 1128 HP.
Once in a while, a vampire would drain a level, but it's no big deal, your
final score is a function of your real XP (i.e. earned by killing monsters) and
not a function of your apparent XP (including wraith corpses and gain level
potions' boosts, and Vampires' drains).
I guess I had exterminated most of the zombies, for the bell began to summon
non-undead monsters...

Anyway, after a few hours I got so bored, I did not notice I was satiated and
choked on... a rothe corpse! :)

Is that undead summoning not too powerful? It looks like an abuse of the same 
kind as polypiling, though it has  no limits.(It could be compared with the
"throw that item in a shop" trick too...though shopkeepers have a limited
amount of money, whereas the number of wraiths in stock is pretty large!).

Anyway, I was just above medusa's level: when things get boring. (Actually they
really get boring once you enter hell): I ascended twice, and I remember my
trips down and back up Hell were really tedious, there was almost no thrill.
 I remember soe. said fort ludios was boring too, I must agree with him, though
the concept is fun:getting into Fort Knox is challenging, but killing MASSES of
wimpy guards to do so isn't.. 
 I think nethack would improve if there were less monsters, and may be less hell
levels, but more powerful monsters. Even the Demon princes are a piece of cake
with Vorpal. (By the way, the end level could be a challenge, if it was not
so easy to map and teleport to your altar! WHY IS TELEPORTING ALLOWED THERE?)
 I'am actually not frustrated to have lost a 1128hp character to a stupid death:
his journey to ascension would have lacked the thrill of the first levels:
I mean the only times I have to engrave Elbereth, or flee, or think real hard
to find how to use my equipment at its best to cope with a tough situation
is in the first levels of the dungeons of Doom and the gnomish mines. 

 Does anybody really enjoys the game after entrance in the Gehenom?
I guess I would if I went there unprepared, but with the WoW in the castle
level, I always enter that part of the game with SoR, GDSM, sleep res. a low
AC and quite a lot of HP. (actually, in my ascending games, I did not have
that many hp, but now that I know that the bell trick is really easy...).

I am looking forward to read your comments, please don't  flame like crazy or
write despising stuff like "if you don't like it, leave it"; NH is a real great
game, but I was just wondering how to make Gehenom less boring.

